    "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability Involving Mutually Exclusive Events",
    "problem": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events. Given that $P(B)=\\frac{1}{15}$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{3}{5},$ find $P(A).$",
    "worked_solution": "If $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events, then $P(A\\cap B)=0.$ \n\nTherefore, by the addition law, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B) \\\\ P(A) & =P(A\\cup B)-P(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
